  CVE-2025-36597|2026-02-17T20:22:04.173|2026-02-18T17:51:53.510|4.7|MEDIUM|CWE-22|N/A|false|Dell Avamar, versions prior to 19.12 with patch 338905, contains an Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal') vulnerability in the Security. A high privileged attacker with remote access could potentially exploit this vulnerability, leading to information disclosure.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-36597
  CVE-2025-36243|2026-02-17T20:22:03.890|2026-02-18T19:09:03.853|5.4|MEDIUM|CWE-918|N/A|false|IBM Concert 1.0.0 through 2.1.0 is vulnerable to server-side request forgery (SSRF). This may allow an authenticated attacker to send unauthorized requests from the system, potentially leading to network enumeration or facilitating other attacks.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-36243
  CVE-2025-33130|2026-02-17T20:22:03.723|2026-02-20T21:01:45.280|6.5|MEDIUM|CWE-120|N/A|false|IBM DB2 Merge Backup for Linux, UNIX and Windows 12.1.0.0 could allow an authenticated user to cause the program to crash due to a buffer being overwritten when it is allocated on the stack.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-33130
