  CVE-2025-27903|2026-02-17T20:22:02.543|2026-02-26T18:14:21.517|5.9|MEDIUM|CWE-319|N/A|false|IBM DB2 Recovery Expert for LUW 5.5 Interim Fix 002 IBM Db2 Recovery Expert for Linux, UNIX and Windows transmits data in a cleartext communication channel that could allow an attacker to obtain sensitive information using man in the middle techniques.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-27903
  CVE-2025-27901|2026-02-17T20:22:02.370|2026-02-25T19:02:23.040|6.5|MEDIUM|CWE-644|N/A|false|IBM DB2 Recovery Expert for LUW 5.5 Interim Fix 002 IBM Db2 Recovery Expert for Linux, UNIX and Windows is vulnerable to HTTP header injection, caused by improper validation of input by the HOST headers.  This could allow an attacker to conduct various attacks against the vulnerable system, including cross-site scripting, cache poisoning or session hijacking.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-27901
  CVE-2025-27900|2026-02-17T20:22:02.207|2026-02-26T18:04:54.583|6.8|MEDIUM|CWE-601|N/A|false|IBM DB2 Recovery Expert for LUW 5.5 Interim Fix 002 could allow a remote attacker to conduct phishing attacks, using an open redirect attack. By persuading a victim to visit a specially crafted Web site, a remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability to spoof the URL displayed to redirect a user to a malicious Web site that would appear to be trusted. This could allow the attacker to obtain highly sensitive information or conduct further attacks against the victim.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-27900
  CVE-2025-27899|2026-02-17T20:22:02.050|2026-02-26T16:33:06.560|5.3|MEDIUM|CWE-526|N/A|false|IBM DB2 Recovery Expert for LUW 5.5 Interim Fix 002 discloses sensitive information in an environment variable that could aid in further attacks against the system.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-27899
  CVE-2025-27898|2026-02-17T20:22:01.883|2026-02-26T16:33:33.923|6.3|MEDIUM|CWE-613|N/A|false|IBM DB2 Recovery Expert for LUW 5.5 Interim Fix 002 does not invalidate session after a timeout which could allow an authenticated user to impersonate another user on the system.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-27898
  CVE-2025-13108|2026-02-17T20:22:01.587|2026-02-26T23:11:08.460|5.5|MEDIUM|NVD-CWE-noinfo|N/A|false|IBM DB2 Merge Backup for Linux, UNIX and Windows 12.1.0.0 could allow an attacker to access sensitive information in memory due to the buffer not properly clearing resources.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-13108
  CVE-2023-38265|2026-02-17T20:22:00.460|2026-02-23T13:10:40.050|5.3|MEDIUM|CWE-548|N/A|false|IBM Cloud Pak System 2.3.3.6, 2.3.3.7, 2.3.4.0, 2.3.4.1, and 2.3.5.0 could disclose folder location information to an unauthenticated attacker that could aid in further attacks against the system.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-38265
